    "description": {
      "value": "<p class=\"feature\">The [[lookup @name lowercase]] randomly shoots one of the following magical rays at a target it can see within 120 feet of itself (roll [[/r 1d10]]; reroll if the beholder has already used that ray during this turn):</p><details><summary><strong>Eye Rays</strong></summary><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>1: Charm Ray.</strong> <em>Wisdom Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=dcpGMW2jBewtY5lx]]. <em>Failure:</em> [[/damage average activity=dcpGMW2jBewtY5lx]] damage, and the target has the &amp;Reference[Charmed apply=false] condition for [[lookup @duration.value activity=dcpGMW2jBewtY5lx]] [[lookup @duration.units activity=dcpGMW2jBewtY5lx]] or until it takes damage. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>2: Paralyzing Ray.</strong> <em>Constitution Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=EZ5rsyCFKBY3TWww]]. <em>Failure:</em> The target has the &amp;Reference[Paralyzed apply=false] condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After [[lookup @duration.value activity=EZ5rsyCFKBY3TWww]] [[lookup @duration.units activity=EZ5rsyCFKBY3TWww]], it succeeds automatically.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>3: Fear Ray.</strong> <em>Wisdom Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=aMfevxGsYy5swVDA]]. <em>Failure:</em> [[/damage average activity=aMfevxGsYy5swVDA]] damage, and the target has the &amp;Reference[Frightened apply=false] condition until the end of its next turn. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>4: Slowing Ray.</strong> <em>Constitution Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=lq2AtXFOVBz6IHMh]]. <em>Failure:</em> [[/damage average activity=lq2AtXFOVBz6IHMh]] damage. Until the end of the target’s next turn, the target’s Speed is halved; the target can’t take &amp;Reference[Reaction]{Reactions}; and it can take either an action or a &amp;Reference[BonusAction] on its turn, not both. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>5: Enervation Ray.</strong> <em>Constitution Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=9srzVFm9txeDeMFf]]. <em>Failure:</em> [[/damage average activity=9srzVFm9txeDeMFf]] damage, and the target has the &amp;Reference[Poisoned apply=false] condition until the end of its next turn. While Poisoned, the target can’t regain Hit Points. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>6: Telekinetic Ray.</strong> <em>Strength Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=a5zT8E1cS4yBVodK]] (the target succeeds automatically if it is Gargantuan). <em>Failure:</em> The [[lookup @name lowercase]] moves the target up to [[lookup @target.template.size activity=a5zT8E1cS4yBVodK]] [[lookup @target.template.units activity=a5zT8E1cS4yBVodK]]. in any direction. The target has the &amp;Reference[Restrained apply=false] condition until the start of the [[lookup @name lowercase]]’s next turn or until the beholder has the Incapacitated condition. The [[lookup @name lowercase]] can also exert fine control on objects with this ray, such as manipulating a tool or opening a door or container.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>7: Sleep Ray.</strong> <em>Wisdom Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=CSKrXM1Pkhlf23et]] (the target succeeds automatically if it is a Construct or an Undead). <em>Failure:</em> The target has the &amp;Reference[Unconscious apply=false] condition for [[lookup @duration.value activity=CSKrXM1Pkhlf23et]] [[lookup @duration.units activity=CSKrXM1Pkhlf23et]]. The condition ends if the target takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>8: Petrification Ray.</strong> <em>Constitution Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=q67AgIfRplRO2e9p]]. <em>First Failure:</em> The target has the &amp;Reference[Restrained apply=false] condition and repeats the save at the end of its next turn if it is still Restrained, ending the effect on itself on a success. <em>Second Failure:</em> The target has the &amp;Reference[Petrified apply=false] condition instead of the Restrained condition.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>9: Disintegration Ray.</strong> <em>Dexterity Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=A5PdqZCq1yeIN8m4]]. <em>Failure:</em> [[/damage average activity=A5PdqZCq1yeIN8m4]] damage. If the target is a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force, a [[lookup @target.template.size activity=A5PdqZCq1yeIN8m4]]-[[lookup @target.template.units activity=A5PdqZCq1yeIN8m4]]. [[lookup @target.template.type capitalize activity=A5PdqZCq1yeIN8m4]] of it disintegrates into dust. <em>Success:</em> Half damage. <em>Failure or Success:</em> If the target is a creature and this damage reduces it to 0 Hit Points, it disintegrates into dust.</p><p class=\"feature-trait\"><strong>10: Death Ray.</strong> <em>Dexterity Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=yjLvFKZIWfUCIT73]]. <em>Failure:</em> [[/damage average activity=yjLvFKZIWfUCIT73]] damage. <em>Success:</em> [[lookup @damage.onSave capitalize activity=yjLvFKZIWfUCIT73]] damage. <em>Failure or Success:</em> The target dies if the ray reduces it to 0 Hit Points.</p></details>",
      "chat": ""
    },
